# shell: desktop
# Q-028/Q-031/Q-032: a saved search can be a TEMPLATE -- a panel filled in
# rather than a search run -- and the Queries menu offers every template
# above the searches that were actually run.  The panel had one Save button
# and no way to reach anything it had ever saved.
key f ctrl
wait 6
key z
key q
key x
wait 2
note first use has created the default template beside the second save action
click 570 404
wait 3
click 580 431
wait 4
expect-status template
note a letter more, so the run is a different search from the template
key y
wait 2
note running it leaves a record of its own, marked temporary
key Return
wait 20
key f ctrl
wait 6
note the menu now has both, the template ABOVE the run
click 570 404
wait 4
click 630 459
wait 4
expect-status template
click 570 404
wait 4
click 630 494
wait 4
expect-status query
quit
